      "content": {
        "title": "Calendar",
        "month": "2025-12",
        "events": {
          "10": {
            "title": "Nobel Prize Day",
            "description": "Nobel Prize Day is on December 10th. It celebrates[称える] the Nobel Prizes[賞] given to people who help the world in important[重要] ways[方法].\n\nAlfred Nobel was a scientist[科学者] from Sweden. He used his money for the prizes. The prizes are for:\n\nPeace[平和]\n\nScience[科学]\n\nMedicine[医学]\n\nLiterature[文学]\n\nEconomics[経済学]\n\nIt is a day to think about people who help the world.",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473209_2687.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473211_6656.jpg"
          },
          "14": {
            "title": "Hanukkah",
            "description": "Hanukkah is a Jewish[ユダヤ人の] celebration that begins on December 14th. It lasts for eight days[8日間].\n\nIt remembers a miracle[奇跡] from a long time ago. There was only a little oil[油], but the light stayed on for eight days.\n\nFamilies light a special candle holder[ろうそく立て] called a menorah[メノーラー]. Each night, they light one more candle.\n\nPeople eat special foods, play a small spinning toy[回るおもちゃ] called a dreidel[ドレイドル], and spend time with family[家族].\n\nHanukkah is a time of light[光], hope[希望], and joy[喜び].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473212_7064.jpg",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473214_5692.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473215_1432.jpg"
          },
          "16": {
            "title": "Las Posadas",
            "description": "Las Posadas is a celebration that starts on December 16th. It is celebrated in Mexico[メキシコ].\n\nIt remembers the story[物語] of Mary[マリア] and Joseph[ヨセフ] looking for a place to stay before Jesus was born.\n\nFamilies and friends walk together and sing special[特別な] songs. Children often hit a piñata[ピニャータ], which is a colorful shape filled with candy[お菓子].\n\nLas Posadas is a time for friends[友だち], family[家族], and fun[楽しい時間].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473217_7791.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473219_8458.jpg"
          },
          "22": {
            "title": "Dongzhi Festival",
            "description": "The Dongzhi Festival is on December 22nd. It is a celebration from China[中国].\n\nDongzhi is the day with the shortest[一番短い] daylight of the year. After this day, the sunlight[日光] becomes longer again.\n\nFamilies come together and eat special[特別な] foods. In China, many people eat tangyuan[湯円], which are sweet rice balls. In Taiwan, people also eat dumplings[餃子].\n\nThe Dongzhi Festival is a time for family[家族], warmth[あたたかさ], and good health[健康].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473221_6625.webp"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473222_444.webp"
          },
          "24": {
            "title": "Christmas Eve",
            "description": "Christmas Eve is on December 24th. It is the night before Christmas[クリスマス].\n\nMany families spend time together and eat a special[特別な] dinner. Some people go to church[教会]. Children often get excited because Santa Claus[サンタクロース] may bring presents[プレゼント].\n\nPeople enjoy lights, music[音楽], and a warm holiday feeling[休日の気分].\n\nChristmas Eve is a time for relaxing[リラックス] with family[家族].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473223_6396.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473225_3645.jpg"
          },
          "25": {
            "title": "Christmas Day",
            "description": "Christmas Day is on December 25th. It celebrates the birth[誕生] of Jesus[イエス] for many Christians[キリスト教徒].\n\nChildren often open presents[プレゼント] in the morning. Families eat a special[特別な] meal together. Many people enjoy relaxing[リラックス], watching movies[映画], or spending time with family[家族] and friends[友だち].\n\nChristmas Day is a time of joy[喜び], sharing[分け合い], and warm feelings[あたたかい気持ち].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473227_1953.jpg",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473229_536.jpg",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473230_4689.jpg",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473232_2587.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473233_3359.jpg"
          },
          "26": {
            "title": "Boxing Day",
            "description": "Boxing Day is on December 26th. It is celebrated in the UK[イギリス], Canada[カナダ], Australia[オーストラリア], and other countries.\n\nA long time ago, rich[金持ち] people gave boxes[箱] of food or money to people who needed help.\n\nToday, Boxing Day is a relaxing day[休む日]. Many people visit family[家族] or friends[友だち], eat leftover[残り物] Christmas food, or go shopping[買い物] because stores have big sales[セール].\n\nBoxing Day is a day to rest[休む] or have fun[楽しむ].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473235_2385.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473235_5149.jpg"
          },
          "31": {
            "title": "New Year's Eve",
            "description": "New Year’s Eve is on December 31st. It is the last day of the year. Many people have parties[パーティー], eat a special[特別な] dinner, and watch fireworks[花火]. Some families wait together until midnight[真夜中].\n\nIn many countries, New Year’s Eve is a fun night with friends[友だち], music[音楽], and celebration[お祝い].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473237_5626.webp",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473239_9590.jpg",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473243_8715.png",
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473248_4284.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473251_2933.webp"
          },
          "01": {
            "title": "World AIDS Day",
            "description": "World AIDS Day is a day to learn about HIV/AIDS[エイズウイルス／エイズ] and to support people who live with it. Many people wear a red ribbon[赤いリボン] to show care[思いやり] and understanding[理解].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473252_4215.png"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473253_6083.png"
          },
          "02": {
            "title": "International Day for the Abolition of Slavery",
            "description": "This day teaches about the history[歴史] of slavery[奴隷制度] and reminds[思い出させる] us that some people around the world are still treated unfairly[不公平に] or forced to work. It teaches us to respect freedom[自由] and human rights[人権].",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473254_7111.webp"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473255_9017.webp"
          },
          "03": {
            "title": "International Day of Persons with Disabilities",
            "description": "This day helps people learn about disabilities[障害] and how to make the world more accessible[利用しやすい]. It reminds us to treat everyone with kindness[優しさ] and respect[尊重].\n\n\n下の画像に、ユニバーサルデザインがいくつ見つかりますか？",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473256_3623.webp"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473257_8568.webp"
          },
          "05": {
            "title": "Krampusnacht / Krampus Night",
            "description": "Krampus Night is celebrated in Austria[オーストリア] and some other European countries. Krampus[クランプス] is a scary creature[怖い生き物] from old stories. People wear costumes and walk in the streets. It is part of traditional[伝統的] winter celebrations before Christmas.",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473258_9739.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473259_9514.jpg"
          },
          "08": {
            "title": "Bodhi Day",
            "description": "Bodhi Day is the day Buddhists remember when the Buddha became very wise.\nHe sat under a big tree called the Bodhi Tree, thought deeply about the world, and learned how to live a peaceful and kind life.\n\n菩提日は、仏教徒が仏陀が深い悟りを得た日を記念する日です。\n仏陀は菩提樹と呼ばれる大きな木の根元に座り、世界の真理について深く思索を重ね、平和で慈愛に満ちた生き方を悟りました。",
            "images": [
              "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473261_6283.jpg"
            ],
            "image": "assets/images/extracted/img_1765233473262_7047.jpg"
          }
        }
      },
      "createdAt": "2025-12-06T10:57:50.968Z"
